worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_code_synthesis.js"
  ceiling 815
  rationale "Browser twins of the issue #1177 composers that build an artifact from a natural-language description: regular expressions and single-SELECT SQL (with GROUP BY and HAVING for an aggregate and JOIN on a stated shared column, #1177 R3; tokens from the lowercased prompt so identifiers keep underscores). `handleRegexSynthesis` / `handleSqlSynthesis` mirror the Rust handlers in rust/src/solver_handlers/{regex,sql}_synthesis.rs; the `try*` bindings pass the lowercased prompt as `normalized`, as the native dispatcher does. JavaScript-first twin of native handler keys (regex_synthesis, sql_synthesis), added under R997-R999 (2026-10-06); growth is the ported handler, not silent regrowth. Ceiling moved 812 to 815 for issue #1177 R2 (2026-10-07): the composed regex is matched against positive and negative examples derived from the same constraints and the result fills the template's execution slot, as rust/src/solver_handlers/regex_witness.rs does natively."
